---
/**
 * Comparison table for the self-hosted spectrum.
 * Isolated from .prose so cell padding and alignment stay intact.
 */
---

<figure class="not-prose my-10">
  <div
    class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
    <table class="w-full min-w-[40rem] table-fixed border-collapse text-left">
      <caption class="sr-only">
        Self-hosted spectrum from BYOC to air-gapped
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-800/80">
          <th
            scope="col"
            class="w-[22%] px-5 py-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
            <span class="sr-only">Dimension</span>
          </th>
          <th
            scope="col"
            class="w-[26%] px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            BYOC
          </th>
          <th
            scope="col"
            class="w-[26%] px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Customer-controlled environment
          </th>
          <th
            scope="col"
            class="w-[26%] px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
            Air-gapped
          </th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <tr class="border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700">
          <th
            scope="row"
            class="px-5 py-4 align-top text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
            Infrastructure
          </th>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">
            Customer cloud. Vendor often provisions it.
          </td>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">Customer controls the environment.</td
          >
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">
            Customer owns it, fully isolated.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr
          class="border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-slate-800/40">
          <th
            scope="row"
            class="px-5 py-4 align-top text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
            Application lifecycle
          </th>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">Vendor operates the app.</td>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">Customer or vendor.</td>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">Fully customer operated.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700">
          <th
            scope="row"
            class="px-5 py-4 align-top text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
            Vendor access
          </th>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">
            Scoped. Constrained channel. Feels like SaaS for the buyer.
          </td>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">Negotiated per customer.</td>
          <td class="px-5 py-4 align-top">None.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    The self-hosted spectrum. Most deals sit in the middle.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
